99	// Tubular frame from cross-sections. Each station { x, w (half width), z: [floor, sill, top] } has six nodes (left/right ×
100	// three levels), braced into a rigid ring. Each bay between stations: longitudinals, a diagonal in every side panel and in
101	// the floor, and optionally in the top. door: "high" keeps the full-height side truss (300 SL); "low" cuts it down to the
102	// sill, as a conventional door opening would (no top rail, no upper side diagonal); a station between two such bays
103	// then has no top ring either. node(s, side, level): side 0 = left (+y), 1 = right (−y); level 0 floor, 1 sill, 2 top.
104	export function tubeFrame(stations, bays, EA) {
